@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Help & FAQ";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] =
        "Find answers about calorie targets, food logging, portions, saved meals, themes and Comfy Capy customisation.";
    ViewData["CanonicalUrl"] = "https://calories.comfycapy.com/Help";
    ViewData["Robots"] = "index,follow";
}

<div class="content-page">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">Help &amp; FAQ</p>
    <h1>How can we help?</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        New to Comfy Capy or something not making sense? You might find the answer here.
    </p>

    <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
        <details open>
            <summary>How do I get my daily calorie target?</summary>
            <p>
                Complete your <a asp-page="/Profile/Index">Profile</a> and Comfy Capy can estimate a
                daily calorie target using your details, activity level and goal. If you already
                have a target you'd rather use, you can set your own instead.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Where does the food information come from?</summary>
            <p>
                Food search includes UK and US food data. UK searches use data from the UK's
                Composition of Foods Integrated Dataset (CoFID), while US searches use USDA
                FoodData Central. You can switch between them when searching for a food, or create
                your own custom foods whenever you need to.
            </p>
            <p>
                Food databases and user-entered foods can contain mistakes or differences between
                products, so it's always worth checking information that's important to you.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What are portions?</summary>
            <p>
                Portions make it easier to log food in amounts that actually make sense to you,
                such as a slice, bowl or serving, instead of reaching for the kitchen scales every
                time. Foods can also be logged using exact measurements when you prefer.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What are approximate portions?</summary>
            <p>
                If you don't know the exact amount you ate, that's okay. Approximate portions let
                you choose a small, medium or large amount using the food's serving information as
                a starting point. They're there for the times when a useful estimate is better
                than not logging at all.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What are Saved Meals?</summary>
            <p>
                Saved Meals are for combinations of foods you eat regularly. You can create one
                from your Diary and use it again later, saving you from adding the same foods one
                by one every time.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Can I copy what I logged yesterday?</summary>
            <p>
                Yep. Your Diary has a <strong>Copy previous day</strong> option for days when what
                you're eating looks suspiciously familiar. It copies the previous day's entries
                into the current day, where you can make any changes you need.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Will editing a food change my old Diary entries?</summary>
            <p>
                No. Comfy Capy keeps the food and nutrition information that applied when you
                logged an entry. If you edit the original food later, your previous Diary entries
                stay as they were.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>How do themes and Capy customisation work?</summary>
            <p>
                Head to <a asp-page="/Customisation">Customise Capy</a> to change your Capy's
                appearance and choose between Light, Dark and System themes. When you're signed
                in, your choices are saved to your account so they'll still be there when you
                come back.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What if I can't confirm my email or sign in?</summary>
            <p>
                You can <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/ResendEmailConfirmation">resend your confirmation email</a>
                or <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/ForgotPassword">reset your password</a>.
                If you use two-factor authentication and can't access your authenticator app,
                you can sign in using one of your saved recovery codes.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details id="nutrition-estimates">
            <summary>Are calorie and nutrition figures medical advice?</summary>
            <p>
                No. Calorie targets, TDEE estimates and nutrition information in Comfy Capy are
                provided for general information and tracking. They're estimates, and food data
                can sometimes be incomplete or inaccurate.
            </p>
            <p>
                Comfy Capy isn't a substitute for medical or professional dietary advice. If you
                have medical or specialised dietary needs, including during pregnancy, for an
                eating disorder, or for a condition affected by nutrition, please speak to an
                appropriately qualified professional.
            </p>
        </details>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-4">
        Still stuck? <a asp-page="/Feedback">Send us some feedback</a> and let us know what's going
        wrong. Please don't include passwords, recovery codes, medical details or other sensitive
        information.
    </p>
</div>